  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is implicated in the regulation of NCI-H446 through a multi-step mechanism involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases, which are targeted by both Corticatic Acid E and 2,3,24-Trihydroxy-12-ursen-28-oic acid. These kinases are likely involved in cellular signaling pathways that influence the behavior of NCI-H446, a cell line that may exhibit altered signaling or metabolic activity under these conditions. The presence of multiple targets, including a protein kinase that is also a target of another compound, suggests a potential role in modulating cellular processes that could be relevant to the disease state of NCI-H446. The integration of these targets highlights the possibility that Corticatic Acid E exerts its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving kinase inhibition or other signaling modulations. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Corticatic Acid E and NCI-H446, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
